    sections: [
      {
        type: 'about',
        tabLabel: 'About',
        pages: [
          {
            title: 'Humbug',
            subtitle: 'Perfect Information Whist',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Humbug is a minimalist 18th-century trick-taking game for two players, representing the simplest possible adaptation of Whist. It is unique because both players are dealt the entire deck, making it a game of perfect information (after the initial overview) and a rigorous test of memory and card counting.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Documented in London publications as early as 1793 (e.g., The Sporting Magazine). It was designed as a high-stakes gambling game for two people who wanted the rigor of Whist without needing partners.',
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Setup',
            subtitle: 'Table, deck, equipment, and deal',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Exactly two players. Humbug was designed as a high-stakes two-hand whist variant for two people who wanted the rigor of Whist without partners; it is documented in London publications from the 1790s (e.g. The Sporting Magazine).',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Standard 52-card deck. Ranking: A (High) to 2 (Low).',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Standard 52-card deck. Ranking: A (High) to 2 (Low).',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Deal all 52 cards, one at a time. The final card (belonging to the dealer) is turned up to determine the Trump suit. Both players then layout their hand face-up by suit to see the complete game state.',
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Variations',
            subtitle: 'Known ways this game changes',
            content: [
