    description: 'Humbug is a minimalist 18th-century trick-taking game for two players, representing the simplest possible adaptation of Whist. It is unique because both players are dealt the entire deck, making it a game of perfect information (after the initial overview) and a rigorous test of memory and card counting.',
    tags: [
      'card-game',
      'trick-taking',
      'social',
    ],
    comingSoon: false,
    minPlayers: 2,
    maxPlayers: 2,
    routePath: 'humbug',
    LLM: 'Game: Humbug (Perfect Information 2-Player Whist). Setup: 52-card deck, 26 cards each, all face-up. Trump: Final card determines trump suit. Gameplay: 52 tricks, non-dealer leads first. Follow suit if able; else any card. Highest suit card or trump wins trick. Scoring: Win >26 tricks = win deal. Revoke (fail to follow) = lose 3 tricks. Strategic depth: Perfect information requires optimal play calculation.',
    Player: 'Welcome to Humbug, the 18th-century perfect information whist game. You and your opponent each get 26 cards, all laid out face-up before play. No hidden informationâ€”you know exactly what each player holds. The trump suit is set by the final card. Play 52 tricks, follow suit if able, and win more than 26 tricks to claim victory.',
    tagline: 'All cards face-up. All cards known. Win 27 tricks and claim victory.',
    gameCategory: 'Trick-taking',
    subcategory: 'Trick-taking',
    playerMode: 'multiplayer',
    difficulty: 'Expert',
    duration: '15-20 minutes',
    origin: 'England',
    originName: 'Humbug',
    deck: 'Standard 52-card deck',
    alsoKnownAs: [
      'Two-Player Whist',
      'Perfect Information Whist',
      '18th-Century Humbug',
      'English Humbug',
    ],
    playersDisplay: '2',
